@flexiarg agency/consult-route-via-bell
@title Route a Bounded Question to a Named Peer Agent
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 2 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-FXOMDp turn-iSo2M1; first proposed for: An operator orchestrates several agents over an async bell transport and mid-task needs input from a specific peer rather than a work product.
@why [orchestration/recorded-handoff]

! conclusion: Tell the current agent to bell the named peer asking for input on the specific issue — recipient and scope travel in one sentence.

  + IF:
    The next step depends on another agent's judgement on one identified issue, and that agent can be reached by bell.

  + HOWEVER:
    A full handoff (spec, acceptance bar, gates) is overkill for a question, yet an unscoped 'any thoughts?' invites drift; the ask must be routed to the right agent and bounded to the issue at hand.

  + THEN:
    Tell the current agent to bell the named peer asking for input on the specific issue — recipient and scope travel in one sentence.

  + BECAUSE:
    It narrows the handoff to its consultation case: same modeled-dispatch discipline, but the deliverable is input on a named issue, not code under gates.
